{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"bob-cli-ir.7.1:000055:note_appended:bob-cli-ir.7.1:5c50d35ca995055c7b51d760efbf582458d1cad6f5e6c33deeadf98367f876cd","timestamp":"2026-11-09T11:21:56Z","actor":"bob-cli-ir.7.1.land","operation":"note_appended","issue_id":"bob-cli-ir.7.1","payload":{"kind":"note_appended","entry":"Lander triage (bob-cli-ir.7.1.land): no child phase recorded any PROPOSED FOLLOW-UP entry, so no /sase_new_task filings were needed. Integration: the only non-epic commit since the epic started is 5e49fa5e (bob-cli-ir.10.1.1, capture-complete -F/--record-field + record.edit); its update-item behavior is folded into the remediation tale, not a separate task. Reviewer findings declined with reasons: (1) current/before values go through validate_field_values, so stored relative-date words and comma-bearing list members are normalized — declined because bob records check uses the same stored-value validator (shared-validator rule); (2) plan_update returns no historical warnings when a supplied field is invalid — declined because those warnings come from the renderer and the refused update already reports its typed error; (3) records new/update -s shell completion emits KEY= and KEY=value rows together — declined because the completion protocol passes no current word and shells prefix-filter; (4) human records update -d prints Markdown without warnings — matches records new; (5) 12641768 bumped GRAMMAR_REVISION 20->21 without a feat(capture)! subject — landed history is immutable and same-day 1c4939b9 feat(records)! already marks the release breaking. Remaining epic-caused gaps (stale collision copy, record_value need on optional-empty updates, update recovery draft dropping parent note, update record.title falling back to note text, record_target rows with grammar-unaddressable stems, symlink alias targets, -F empty bullet on update items, missing record_target key docs, missing parse/CLI unknown/ambiguous target tests) are planned as one tale that ends with this epic's closeout."}}
